## Address hypothesis and prior art

Candidate only: physical zero, possible length 0x20000. Qualcomm's APQ8064
LM80-P0598-1 Rev B datasheet section3.1.1 says ARM7 RPM is the primary boot
processor; figure4-1 places its 128KiB ROM at zero. This is related-chip
primary documentation, not proof of MSM8930 readability.
https://www.qualcomm.com/content/dam/qcomm-martech/dm-assets/documents/snapdragon_600_apq_8064_data_sheet.pdf

Contemporaneous SCH-I535/MSM8960 viewmem extraction report:
https://xdaforums.com/t/r-d-unlock-bootloaders.1769411/post-30084661
https://xdaforums.com/t/r-d-unlock-bootloaders.1769411/post-30086307
No exact MSM8930/Express ROM binary with authenticated chip revision/address/
size/hash provenance was found. Broad edl APQ806x/MSM8930 configuration at
0x100000 overlaps this handset's live RPM interface at108000 and is not a
sufficient basis for probing that range.

