## Reader tests and inspection

Host cargo test --locked --manifest-path tools/physread/Cargo.toml: 11 pass.
Same tests for armv7-unknown-linux-musleabihf under qemu-arm: 12 pass,
including a real memfd-backed mapping crossing a page boundary, and a
32-bit musl test proving offset2^44 is rejected rather than truncated by mmap2.
No unit test opens /dev/mem.
cargo fmt --check, cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings, git diff --check:
all pass. Static ARMv7 release build passes.
Reader retained as target/pbl-lab/physread:
  361752 bytes
  SHA256 0d857360bd2c0289acd0e6d9d583f5f754757b69c7471a72ae1a60e94d2e45db

A review concern about mmap2 high-offset wrapping was checked against musl:
https://git.musl-libc.org/cgit/musl/tree/src/mman/mmap.c
Musl checks OFF_MASK and returns EINVAL before syscall argument narrowing.
The new ARM32 regression test covers that behavior; no duplicate libc guard
was added. Output preserves native memory bytes. O_RDONLY|O_SYNC and
PROT_READ|MAP_SHARED; aligned volatile32 loads; no physical writes.

Pocketboot spawn_raw_command combines stdout/stderr and has no shell-v2 exit
status. The documented hardware procedure therefore captures binary output,
stderr and exit status in separate RAM-backed files before host retrieval.
Otherwise an error message could be mistaken for dump bytes.

## Next action, not yet authorized/executed

RAM-boot the diagnostic image on the selected handset, verify its release,
SoC/CPU/memory identities and devmem, then read one word at physical zero.
A read may bus-fault, hang or reset the handset. No broad scans, register
writes, security-fuse changes or flash writes are part of this experiment.
Only after inspecting the first result should a page/full-window dump be
considered. Stable zeros or plausible disassembly alone are insufficient
ROM provenance. Keep raw binaries local; record any future acquisition
address/size/hash and repeated-read evidence in this notes ref.

